id: ops-release-bash-lastpipe
title: Refuse unsupported Bash lastpipe mode in release changelog hooks
description: Greptile PR #295 discussion 4622238972 on c1e0c80 identifies a release hook that enables Bash lastpipe and then runs a directory change in the final pipeline stage. Locally reproduced in noninteractive Bash and the release hook resolver.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:release",ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-ops#295"
created_at: "2026-11-18T23:25:42.056Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T23:25:43.631Z"
author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Cover the configured Bash mode and confirm default shell pipeline stages and subshells continue to isolate directory changes.
severity: high
environment: Noninteractive Bash with lastpipe enabled
repro_steps: Use shopt -s lastpipe; printf x | cd docs; npm run writer in a Bash hook with a literal writer script in the root manifest.
expected_result: The gate refuses an unsupported execution mode that may change the package directory for the writer.
actual_result: Bash runs the writer in the new directory while resolveChangelogHooks and assertReleaseHookHeadingDate accept the root manifest writer.
files[3]{path,scope}:
  release-changelog-options.ts,project
  release-hook-grammar.ts,project
  test/release-hook-grammar.test.ts,project
body: ""
